it's been a month since we got our hands  on the galaxy buds plus and we've been  testing them comparing them to  comparable ear buds and using them in  the real world here's what we think  about them in who we think should buy  the galaxy buds plus over the other  options out there now before we begin  there were a few things that we're  lacking with the original Galaxy buds  like for example active noise  cancellation poor microphone quality and  latency and we'll get into those things  in just a minute even before we got our  hands on the buds plus we were surprised  that Samsung priced them at $150 only  $20 higher than the original buds  however the old buds are now available  on sale for around $100 or less so we'll  let you guys know if it makes sense to  pay the extra cash for the buds plus  later on in the video the very first  time we tested and heard the buds plus  using the dynamic sound mode we were  blown away by the sound quality and  volume they sounded incredibly good with  very bright highs and there's a really  good reason for it  the bus Plus actually feature two  separate speaker drivers a tweeter for  high frequencies and a woofer for mids  and bass on a lot of other ear buds like  even the air Potts Pro there is only one  driver that has to take care of every  frequency which is quite difficult  compared to having multiple drivers for  this reason the buds plus sound great an  inner sound quality comparison our  conclusion was that they actually sound  a little bit better than the air pods  Pro which we honestly didn't expect  since they're $100 cheaper now of course  that's not the only reason to buy  wireless earbuds so let's get into what  was a bit disappointing the buds plus  now have two microphones instead of one  so we expected better mic quality but  when we compared it to the original buds  we didn't hear much of a difference just  listen to it yourself compared to the  air Potts Pro as well this is a  microphone quality test during a phone  call using the original Galaxy buds this  is a microphone quality test during a  phone call using the new Galaxy buds  Plus this is a microphone quality during  a call with at the airport's pro this a  microphone quality during a call with  the Galaxy buds plus in putting these  tests aside we use them in the real  world through  actual phone calls and we were told that  the quality of the mics on the buds plus  is way behind the ear pods Pro and if  you really think about it  the ear pods have a stem that puts the  mic closer to your mouth  unlike the buds that barely stick out of  your ears so it makes sense why the my  quality would be worse however I really  like that the buds Plus have such a  low-profile design lacking any kind of  stem that sticks out this means you can  change your shirt sweatshirt or even put  on a motorcycle helmet without having to  take your buds out of course using the  ambient mode to make sure you can still  hear your surroundings now getting into  that ambient mode it honestly doesn't  work as well as the transparency mode on  the earpods Pro which makes voices sound  a lot more natural and not tinny like on  the bus plus one missing feature on  these buds is active noise cancellation  but they're obviously much cheaper than  earbuds that pack that feature so I'm  not taking off very many points for that  on the plus side they seal in your ears  pretty well so they do a really good job  of naturally blocking noise but if you  travel a lot on airplanes you should  definitely consider getting earbuds with  active noise cancellation but I think  not a lot of people are flying for a bit  seeing what's going on in the world  right now now there are some benefits of  not having that feature like not having  to pack extra noise cancellation  hardware inside of the buds that take  space away from the batteries now these  buds plus actually pack 85 milliamp hour  batteries compared to 58 on the original  bus which is a huge difference in this  along with improvements in efficiency  gives the buds plus ear buds 11 hours of  battery life compared to only 6 on the  originals this is honestly excellent  blowing away a lot of other ear buds  like the air pods Pro in terms of  battery life in the real world this  makes such a massive difference if you  use them at work it's really nice not to  have to recharge them compared to having  the pop the air Potts Pro back and the  charging case before the end of the work  day and if you include the extra battery  in the case you get 22 hours of total  battery life not only that but charging  speed has improved as well compared to  the originals we also tested out the  buzz plus with an  iPhone 11 Promax and we were surprised  to see that the experience was actually  pretty good  so we recommended people who can't  afford the air Potts Pro to simply go  with the buds plus a big reason for that  is that Samsung just released a new  Galaxy buds Plus app on iOS which gives  you a lot more customized ability and  fine-tuning of sound now one of the  things we tested between the air Potts  pro and the buds plus was latency and we  saw that the air pods were much quicker  in terms of lag time between tapping the  screen and hearing sound for that the  buzz plus have a gaming mode which  reduces latency and while it did help a  lot and we recommend Android users to  use that feature while gaming the air  Potts pro we're still a bit better in  terms of latency we actually made a  video where we compared the buds plus to  the air Potts Pro and the sony WF 1000  XM threes we concluded that Android  users who don't want to spend at least  two hundred and twenty eight dollars on  the Sony's should just go with the bus  plus despite the lack of active noise  cancellation now with all of that said  we've been extremely impressed with the  Galaxy buds Plus and mainly for three  reasons the excellent battery life the  dual speaker drivers and the $150 price  tag gives you such a good balance of  features and with that even though you  can get the original Galaxy buds for  around $100 on sale we would honestly  recommend everyone considering those  buds to just pay the extra cash for the  Galaxy buds plus because they're  honestly that much better if you enjoyed  this video tap like and click the circle  above to subscribe for more videos like  this one and make sure to check out one  of those two videos right over there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]
 

